{"vid":"vbXPcaEQTvg","source":"vbXPcaEQTvg.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.1,"txt":"when you're getting started with tig"},{"t":1.4,"txt":"welding it's nice to have a stash of"},{"t":3.4,"txt":"filler metals that you're going to use"},{"t":5,"txt":"but it can be confusing with all the"},{"t":6.5,"txt":"different numbering systems and"},{"t":8.1,"txt":"different sizes to know what to get so"},{"t":10.2,"txt":"i'm going to break it all down for you"},{"t":11.4,"txt":"in this video hey welcome to the shop"},{"t":13.4,"txt":"let me show you the filler metals that i"},{"t":14.9,"txt":"use the most we'll start off with steel"},{"t":16.9,"txt":"then we'll talk about aluminum stainless"},{"t":18.6,"txt":"steel and even a little bit of braze"},{"t":20.2,"txt":"alloy so first of all with steel there's"},{"t":23.4,"txt":"er70s dash you'll have something after"},{"t":26.2,"txt":"that the most common is er 70s-2 when it"},{"t":29.3,"txt":"comes to tig welding another one that's"},{"t":31.5,"txt":"commonly uh cut is a wire that's often"},{"t":34.2,"txt":"used in mig er-70s-6"},{"t":37.3,"txt":"now the difference between those wires"},{"t":39.1,"txt":"is pretty subtle and it has to do with"},{"t":41.1,"txt":"some of the alloying elements primarily"},{"t":44.1,"txt":"relating to deoxidizing your weld and"},{"t":46.5,"txt":"honestly either one of those"},{"t":48.8,"txt":"will work just fine for most"},{"t":50.6,"txt":"applications you probably won't be able"},{"t":52.1,"txt":"to tell a difference but i typically buy"},{"t":54.1,"txt":"er 70s-2 now it comes in these cut links"},{"t":58.2,"txt":"and it's typically copper colored"},{"t":59.8,"txt":"because it's coated on the outside it's"},{"t":62,"txt":"available in a variety of different"},{"t":63.5,"txt":"sizes now the size that you use"},{"t":66,"txt":"is going to be a little bit of personal"},{"t":67.5,"txt":"preference and typically will relate to"},{"t":69.9,"txt":"the thickness of material you're welding"},{"t":71.5,"txt":"and the size of weld you're trying to"},{"t":72.9,"txt":"put in right because if you're trying to"},{"t":74.3,"txt":"put in a particular"},{"t":76.3,"txt":"size a fillet weld and use really small"},{"t":78.3,"txt":"wire you're going to have to feed a lot"},{"t":80.9,"txt":"of that wire in as you go"},{"t":83.5,"txt":"where a larger wire you might not have"},{"t":85.7,"txt":"to feed quite so much in but on the flip"},{"t":88.4,"txt":"side a larger wire acts as a heat sink"},{"t":91.2,"txt":"which can be good"},{"t":92.6,"txt":"for"},{"t":93.5,"txt":"larger welds but when you get to smaller"},{"t":95.3,"txt":"welds it can make it really difficult to"},{"t":97,"txt":"be able to add it to your puddle"},{"t":99,"txt":"and get a really precise result"},{"t":101.7,"txt":"now the sizes that i use are typically 1"},{"t":104.7,"txt":"16 of an inch and that's right around"},{"t":107.3,"txt":"one and a half millimeters that's what i"},{"t":109.4,"txt":"use for most of the work that i do which"},{"t":111.3,"txt":"is on plates that are right around an"},{"t":113,"txt":"eighth of an inch thick or three"},{"t":114.8,"txt":"millimeters thick"},{"t":116.2,"txt":"but i also like to keep some smaller"},{"t":118.3,"txt":"filler metal around this is forty five"},{"t":120.8,"txt":"thousandths of an inch which is right"},{"t":122.1,"txt":"around one millimeter"},{"t":123.8,"txt":"and this filler metal is really great"},{"t":126.6,"txt":"when i'm getting down to materials that"},{"t":128.6,"txt":"are right around a sixteenth of an inch"},{"t":130.6,"txt":"or"},{"t":131.5,"txt":"you know one and a half millimeters"},{"t":133,"txt":"thick"},{"t":134.4,"txt":"because it gives me just a little bit of"},{"t":136.2,"txt":"control now let's talk a little bit"},{"t":138,"txt":"about aluminum if you're gonna be"},{"t":139.2,"txt":"welding aluminum there are two really"},{"t":141.3,"txt":"common filler materials that are used"},{"t":143.9,"txt":"one is 4043 and the other is 5356."},{"t":148.2,"txt":"now the common size that i get for both"},{"t":150.7,"txt":"of those is three thirty seconds of an"},{"t":152.5,"txt":"inch it's a little bit larger than i'll"},{"t":154.2,"txt":"typically use on steel because aluminum"},{"t":156.9,"txt":"welds tend to take a little bit more"},{"t":159.2,"txt":"filler metal at least that's been my"},{"t":160.7,"txt":"experience 4043 first of all it's a"},{"t":163.1,"txt":"lower strength material"},{"t":165.1,"txt":"it"},{"t":166,"txt":"is very fluid so it'll flow in and"},{"t":168.2,"txt":"typically gives a little bit smoother"},{"t":170,"txt":"bead overall without quite as much of a"},{"t":172.1,"txt":"rippled appearance"},{"t":173.5,"txt":"and drawback of 4043"},{"t":176.7,"txt":"is that"},{"t":178.1,"txt":"if you go to anodize your parts you want"},{"t":180.2,"txt":"to have a color added to them with an"},{"t":182,"txt":"anodized surface"},{"t":183.5,"txt":"you're gonna end up with a bit of a"},{"t":185.9,"txt":"color mismatch most of the time"},{"t":188.6,"txt":"now 53 56 on the other hand is a little"},{"t":192.2,"txt":"bit higher strength in my experience"},{"t":194.2,"txt":"gives typically a little bit shinier"},{"t":196.2,"txt":"weld with more of a stack of dime's"},{"t":198,"txt":"appearance"},{"t":199.1,"txt":"and it will anodize quite well now one"},{"t":201.4,"txt":"of the drawbacks with 5356"},{"t":204.2,"txt":"is prolonged use at an elevated"},{"t":207.8,"txt":"temperature"},{"t":209,"txt":"is likely to result in some issues down"},{"t":212.4,"txt":"inside the material and you can end up"},{"t":213.9,"txt":"with some corrosion or cracking problems"},{"t":216.2,"txt":"for most of the common materials that"},{"t":218.6,"txt":"you'll weld like a 6061"},{"t":221.3,"txt":"aluminum alloy you can use either of"},{"t":223.6,"txt":"these filler metals but aluminum alloys"},{"t":226.3,"txt":"aren't compatible with one another"},{"t":228.1,"txt":"across the board and the reasons for"},{"t":230.3,"txt":"that get very complex but most of the"},{"t":232,"txt":"filler metal manufacturers have a chart"},{"t":233.8,"txt":"out there that you can get if you just"},{"t":235,"txt":"google aluminum filler metal chart"},{"t":237.5,"txt":"you'll find them from"},{"t":239.8,"txt":"esab from hobart you know a lot of those"},{"t":243.2,"txt":"companies you can pull up a big chart"},{"t":246.3,"txt":"and it'll show what aluminum alloy you"},{"t":248.5,"txt":"have and one side of the weld the"},{"t":250.6,"txt":"aluminum alloy you have on the other and"},{"t":253.2,"txt":"which materials are compatible as far as"},{"t":255.7,"txt":"filler metals as well as what kind of"},{"t":257.8,"txt":"properties that to expect when you use"},{"t":259.4,"txt":"that filler metal i use"},{"t":261.6,"txt":"5356 for most of what i do i find it"},{"t":264.6,"txt":"works quite well for me next let's talk"},{"t":266.6,"txt":"about stainless steels now stainless"},{"t":268.2,"txt":"steels there's a wide variety of"},{"t":270.2,"txt":"stainless steels but the most common"},{"t":272.1,"txt":"that you'll probably encounter are 300"},{"t":275.2,"txt":"series stainless steels that means that"},{"t":277.7,"txt":"it has a three digit designator that"},{"t":279.4,"txt":"starts with a three"},{"t":281.2,"txt":"and those are not magnetic they're"},{"t":284.1,"txt":"pretty corrosion resistant and that's"},{"t":286.6,"txt":"because they have an addition of"},{"t":289.1,"txt":"chromium that creates a stable oxide"},{"t":291.5,"txt":"layer on the surface that keeps the iron"},{"t":295,"txt":"in it from reacting with the oxygen and"},{"t":297.6,"txt":"rusting now they also have a significant"},{"t":300.7,"txt":"addition of nickel and that's what makes"},{"t":303.1,"txt":"them non-magnetic and it makes them"},{"t":305.7,"txt":"workable"},{"t":306.9,"txt":"now for these type of materials there"},{"t":309.5,"txt":"are different filler metals available"},{"t":311.4,"txt":"but most of the time when you're welding"},{"t":313.4,"txt":"like a 304 which is really common you"},{"t":316,"txt":"would use a 308 l filler metal another"},{"t":319.9,"txt":"common stainless steel filler material"},{"t":322.4,"txt":"is 309"},{"t":324.4,"txt":"and the difference with 309l is it has a"},{"t":327.2,"txt":"little bit more of that chromium and"},{"t":329.1,"txt":"nickel and that makes it possible to"},{"t":332.5,"txt":"weld a stainless steel to like a regular"},{"t":335.6,"txt":"carbon steel so if you are doing a"},{"t":337,"txt":"dissimilar weld where you're welding you"},{"t":339.4,"txt":"know"},{"t":340.3,"txt":"mild steel to something that's stainless"},{"t":342.6,"txt":"steel that's where that 309 l is going"},{"t":345.3,"txt":"to come in handy but for most work 308l"},{"t":349.4,"txt":"is going to be pretty good now when i'm"},{"t":350.7,"txt":"working with stainless steel it's"},{"t":352.4,"txt":"typically pretty thin stuff"},{"t":354.6,"txt":"and it's right around you know maybe a"},{"t":357,"txt":"sixteenth of an inch one and a half"},{"t":358.2,"txt":"millimeter thick sheet"},{"t":360.1,"txt":"and for that i use this forty five"},{"t":362.9,"txt":"thousandths of an inch or one millimeter"},{"t":365.2,"txt":"filler metal so similar to the steel"},{"t":367.4,"txt":"where i'd use on that thickness"},{"t":369.8,"txt":"thinner material i'll use that on"},{"t":371.4,"txt":"stainless steel as well and that works"},{"t":373.8,"txt":"pretty well for me let's just talk about"},{"t":375.8,"txt":"one more that's come in really handy for"},{"t":377.7,"txt":"me this is silicon bronze it's a brazing"},{"t":379.8,"txt":"alloy now the difference with brazing is"},{"t":382.8,"txt":"instead of actually trying to melt the"},{"t":384.8,"txt":"base metal you will be trying to heat up"},{"t":387.8,"txt":"the base metal in all reality with tig"},{"t":389.6,"txt":"raising sometimes you melt it a little"},{"t":391,"txt":"bit"},{"t":391.7,"txt":"but the goal is just to heat it up and"},{"t":394.5,"txt":"to use that hot material to melt a"